      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186176049/tangent.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function $y=\\tan x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has period $\\pi .$ So, $\\tan (x+n\\pi )=\\tan (x+n\\pi )=\\tan (x+n\\pi )=\\tan (x).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The range of $y=\\tan x$ is $(-\\infty ,+\\infty ).$"
    },
