    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c81a5f48-f7ea-503b-b73b-211329fa1233",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\tan (x+\\pi )=\\tan (x+2n\\pi ).$\n- **II.** The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi $\n- **III.** $\\tan (x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\tan (x+\\frac{2\\pi }{3}).$\n\nIn tangent equalities, consider values of $x$ where both sides are defined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a49339b3-e18f-5272-8cae-3eed62363b1a",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "09df782a-6afa-58c7-8b01-2fb06177e0ca",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "3e07c021-945e-5d42-a95d-ab24cf7dbb4d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
